■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on Management of Firefighting Equipment [Attached Table 6]

Criteria for Imposition of Administrative Fines (Re: Article 48)

1. General criteria

(a) Aggravated criteria for imposition of administrative fines according to the number of violations shall apply where an administrative fine has been imposed for the same violation within the preceding three years. The period shall be calculated by reference to the date on which the administrative fine was imposed for the violation and the date on which the same violation committed again after that disposition was detected.

(b) Where an aggravated fine is imposed under item (a), the occurrence level applied for the aggravated fine shall be the level immediately following the occurrence level of the disposition imposed before the violation (where administrative fines were imposed twice or more within the period under item (a), the highest such occurrence level).

(c) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency or the Mayor/Do Governor may reduce the administrative fine under the individual criteria in paragraph 2 by up to one half in any of the following cases: Provided, That this shall not apply to a violator who is in arrears with administrative fines.

1) Where the violator falls under any subparagraph of Article 2-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Regulation of Violations of Public Order;

2) Where the violator has committed the relevant violation for the first time and is recognized to have conducted the relevant business in an exemplary manner for at least three years;

3) Where circumstances exist such as the violator having suffered a substantial loss of property due to a natural disaster, fire, etc., or the business facing a serious crisis due to deteriorating business conditions;

4) Where the violation is found to have resulted from minor carelessness or an error;

5) Where the violator has received a disposition such as an administrative fine, criminal fine or suspension of business under another Act for the same violation;

6) Where the violator has corrected or eliminated the consequences of the violation;

7) Other cases where reduction of the administrative fine is deemed necessary in consideration of the degree of the violation, the motive for the violation and its consequences, etc.

2. Individual criteria

Administrative fine amounts are expressed in units of 10,000 won.

| Violation | Legal basis | First violation | Second violation | Third or subsequent violation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| (a) A person other than a fire service agency or a public official belonging thereto uses painting and marking identical to those of fire equipment in violation of Article 11 (2) of the Act | Article 48 (1) of the Act | 200 | 400 | 500 |
| (b) A person other than a fire service agency or a public official belonging thereto uses painting and marking similar to those of fire equipment in violation of Article 11 (2) of the Act | Article 48 (1) of the Act | 100 | 200 | 300 |
